 with leading zeros, or `-`, or a path through a scalar). Only own members of objects are followed.
 
 Tests run with `npm test` (Node 22.18+, which runs TypeScript test files directly).
+
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a JSON Patch (an array of
+`add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test` operations) to a document and returns the result
+as a new value; neither argument is mutated and the result shares no structure with them. Operations
+apply in order. It throws an `Error` if the patch is invalid (not an array, unknown `op`, missing or
+invalid `path`, `from` or `value`) or if an operation fails (target missing, array index out of range,
+`move` into its own child, failed `test`); a failed patch returns nothing, so it is all-or-nothing.
+Removing the whole document is rejected. `test` compares by JSON equality (member order is ignored).
